\begin_layout Standard
Point Mutation: A single node of a tree is selected and changed.
 If the node is a function, it is randomly replaced by a new one.
 If it is a variable, its value is genetically optimized, for which purpose
 it is changed with a Gaussian filter.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Branch Mutation: A random node of the tree is selected and the complete
 branch is regenerated.
 This allows even larger changes to occur.
 Furthermore, depending on the length of the new branch, the total number
 of nodes can either increase or decrease.
\end_layout

